  <static seed="65" source="Library/TCNJ/TCNJ_IntroLinearTransformations/problem17.pg">
    <statement><p>Let <m>T : {\mathbb R}^2 \to {\mathbb R}^2</m> be a linear transformation
that sends the vector
<m>\vec{u} =(5,2)</m> into <m>(2,1)</m> and maps  <m>\vec{v}= (1,3)</m> into 
<m>(-1, 3)</m>.</p>
<p>Use properties of a linear transformation to calculate the following.
(Enter your answers as ordered pairs, such as <m>(1,2)</m>, including the parentheses.)</p>
<p><m>T(-4 \vec{u}) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,</p>
<p><m>T(9 \vec{v}) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,</p>
<p><m>T(-4 \vec{u} + 9 \vec{v}) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-8,-4\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-9,27\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-17,23\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>T(-4 \vec{u}) = -4T(\vec{u})=-4(2,1)=(-8,-4)</m>
<m>T(9 \vec{v}) = 9T(\vec{v})=9(1,3)=(-9,27)</m>
<m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned} T(-4 \vec{u} + 9 \vec{v}) \amp = -4T(\vec{u})+9T(\vec{v})\\
\amp =(-8,-4)+($ans21,$ans22)  \\
\amp = ($ans31,$ans32) \end{aligned}}</m></p>
</solution>
